ecard-title"><h2 id="model-scorecard-title">Every model, with its own evaluation population</h2><p class="note">Frozen, weekly rolling, per-game rolling and issued forecasts remain separate. Current-season results describe monitoring; they do not select a champion. Historical seasons only appear when the supplied report contains them.</p><div class="toolbar"><div class="control"><label for="metric-period">Period</label><select id="metric-period"><option value="season">Season</option><option value="week">Week</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="metric-league">League</label><select id="metric-league"><option value="all">Both, separately</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="metric-season">Season end year</label><select id="metric-season"><option value="all">All supplied seasons</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="metric-target">Objective</label><select id="metric-target"><option value="all">All, separately</option><option value="win">Winner probability</option><option value="margin">Point margin</option><option value="total">Point total</option><option value="cover">Spread cover</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="metric-stream">Forecast stream</label><select id="metric-stream"><option value="all">Every supplied stream</option></select></div></div><div class="pager"><p id="metric-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="buttons"><button id="metric-previous" class="secondary" type="button">Previous models</button><button id="metric-next" class="secondary" type="button">Next models</button></div></div><div id="model-metrics"></div><p class="note">Accuracy, log loss, Brier and calibration evaluate probabilities; MAE, RMSE and bias evaluate points. Uncertainty, CRPS, and interval coverage are shown only when authored. A probability for a binary threshold is not an expected margin or total.</p></section><section class="provider-review" id="provider-review" aria-labelledby="provider-review-title"><h2 id="provider-review-title">Our models and all three providers</h2><p class="note">Inspect each provider's eligible games and the exact common-game populations separately. These are authored report values: forecast streams, leagues, seasons, horizons and evidence modes remain distinct.</p><div class="toolbar"><div class="control"><label for="provider-period">Metric period</label><select id="provider-period"><option value="season">Season</option><option value="week">Week</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="provider-cohort">Comparison population</label><select id="provider-cohort"><option value="provider">Each provider's eligible games</option><option value="common">Common games across all three</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="provider-league">Comparison league</label><select id="provider-league"><option value="all">Men and women, separated</option><option value="ncaam">Men</option><option value="ncaaw">Women</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="provider-target">Comparison objective</label><select id="provider-target"><option value="win">Winner probability</option><option value="margin">Point margin</option><option value="total">Point total</option><option value="all">All objectives, separated</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="provider-stream">Comparison model stream</label><select id="provider-stream"><option value="all">Every recorded stream</option></select></div><div class="control" id="provider-week-control" hidden><label for="provider-week">Supplied week</label><select id="provider-week"><option value="all">Every supplied week</option></select></div></div><p class="market-clock-note" id="provider-comparison-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="provider-grid" id="provider-cards"></div><p class="note">A binary spread/total threshold probability is not an expected point margin or total. Unsupported point comparisons and uncertainty intervals stay separate from measured values; no missing value becomes zero.</p><div class="pager"><p id="provider-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="buttons"><button id="provider-previous" class="secondary" type="button">Previous populations</button><button id="provider-next" class="secondary" type="button">Next populations</button></div></div><div id="provider-populations"></div><p class="source-note" id="provider-source-status"></p><h3>Correct and wrong disagreements</h3><p class="note">Counts within each population show how often the model was right when each provider was wrong, and the reverse. Exact supplied records follow below; one game can have several model records. This source inventory has its own scope: choosing common metrics does not infer common membership for these records. These records evaluate prediction disagreements within their stated population.</p><div class="pager"><p id="provider-disagreement-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div class="buttons"><button id="provider-disagreement-previous" class="secondary" type="button">Previous disagreements</button><button id="provider-disagreement-next" class="secondary" type="button">Next disagreements</button></div></div><div id="provider-disagreements"></div><div id="provider-source-audit"></div></section><section class="detail" id="injury-source-section" aria-labelledby="injury-source-title">
